---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import createSlug from "../lib/createSlug"

const posts = (await getCollection("blog")).sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());

const last_posts = posts.slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout title="Hung D. Nguyen" sideBarActiveItemID="home">
  <div class="pb-12 mt-5">
    <!-- <div class="text-xl py-1">Hey there 👋</div> -->
    <div class="text-5xl font-bold text-center">Nguyen Dac Hung</div>
    <div class="text-3xl py-3 italic text-center">Astrophysicist and Digital Story-teller </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-8 mt-6">
      <img 
        src="/index.webp"
        alt="Nguyen Dac Hung"
        class="w-48 h-48 md:w-64 md:h-64 object-cover flex-shrink-0"
      />
      <div class="py-2 text-justify">
      <text class="text-lg">
        I'm a senior at Michigan State University studying Astrophysics and Computational Math. 
        I'm from Hanoi, Vietnam, but I also grew up in London and Beijing. I study the formation 
        and evolution of planetary systems using numerical simulations. Specifically, I'm interested
        in modeling planet forming environments such as protoplanetary disks. I also enjoy sharing my 
        stories through film online. Feel free to check out my work in the socials tab below and 
        connect with me on LinkedIn!
      </text>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8">
      <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nguyen-dac-hung/" target="_blank"> Let's connect!</a>
      <a href="https://www.instagram.com/nd_hung.films/" target="_blank" class="btn btn-outline ml-5">My socials</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/nguy1241" target="_blank" class="btn btn-outline ml-5">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-2">MY RESEARCH 🪐</div>
  </div>

  <div class="py-2">
  <text class="text-lg">
    With numerical simulations, I have done a number of  
    I am interested in the conditions of the protoplanetary disk that lead to the formation of the Earth 
    and the Giant Impact event which formed the Moon.
  </text>
</div>



